<!--
    This file is used by the Qspa framework to determine the list of applications that need to be
    disabled based on the corresponding hardware subsystem enablement on device.
    Developers are requested to add/remove entries along with the corresponding subsystem name
    and the applications along with the qspa propertyValue to disable
    applications. The application will be disabled if the provided
    subsystem's corresponding qspa value on device matches with the propertyvalue mentioned.

    Each <packageinfo> tag corresponds to one app and has the following attributes:

    1. name: The package name as defined in the app's AndroidManifest.xml.
             For duplicate entry of package name, add version number at the end.
             e.g., com.qti.phone , com.qti.phone.2


    2. path: The app's location on the file system.
             a. For apps that have their own directory, e.g., /product/priv-app/Dialer/Dialer.apk,
                this should point to the directory.
             b. For apps that don't, e.g., /product/overlay/TelephonyResCommon_Sys.apk, this should
                point to the apk.

    Example:
    <packages>
        <propertyCheck subsystem="modem">
            <propertyValue value="disabled">
                <packageinfo name="com.android.phone" path="/system/priv-app/TeleService" />
                <packageinfo name="com.android.phone.overlay.common" path="/product/overlay/TelephonyResCommon_Sys.apk" />
                <Other packages if needed/>
            </propertyValue>
            <propertyValue value="enabled">
                <packageinfo name="abc" path="xyz.apk" />
                <Other packages if needed/>
            </propertyValue>
        </propertyCheck>
        <propertyCheck subsystem="audio">
            <propertyValue value="enabled">
                <packageinfo name="abc1" path="xyz1.apk" />
                <Other packages if needed/>
            </propertyValue>
            <propertyValue value="disabled">
                <packageinfo name="abc2" path="xyz2.apk" />
                <Other packages if needed/>
            </propertyValue>
        </propertyCheck>
    This list of applications would be disabled based on ro.boot.vendor.qspa.<subsystem>value on device
-->

